

<% content_for :title, "IFS & Bipolar | Bipolar Sober" %>

<style>
  .ifs-bipolar-page .ifs-copy,
  .ifs-bipolar-page .ifs-parts > div,
  .ifs-bipolar-page .ifs-practice-list > div {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .ifs-bipolar-page .ifs-source {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.75em;
    font-style: normal;
  }
</style>

<main class="ifs-bipolar-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="ifs-bipolar-hero">
    <div class="ifs-bipolar-hero-content">

      <p class="ifs-bipolar-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / PERSPECTIVES / IFS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>BIPOLAR</span>
        <span>THROUGH AN</span>
        <span>IFS LENS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="ifs-bipolar-intro">
        YOU HAVE PARTS.<br>
        NONE OF THEM ARE ALL OF YOU.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / THE BASIC IDEA -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-pink" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-1-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        01 / THE BASIC IDEA
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-1-title">
        YOU ARE<br>
        NOT ONE<br>
        THING.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <blockquote>
        <p>"There are no bad parts."</p>
        <cite class="ifs-source">— Richard C. Schwartz</cite>
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        Internal Family Systems—IFS—uses “parts” to describe different feelings,
        beliefs, fears, and protective patterns. One part may want control while another
        wants escape; one wants sobriety while another wants immediate relief. These
        conflicts can reflect different needs. IFS invites you to understand them with
        curiosity and compassion.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / SELF -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-yellow" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-2-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        02 / SELF
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-2-title">
        WHO'S<br>
        BEHIND THE<br>
        NOISE?
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        In IFS, Self-leadership means approaching your inner experience with these eight
        qualities:
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-self-grid">

        <span>CURIOSITY</span>
        <span>COMPASSION</span>
        <span>CALM</span>
        <span>CLARITY</span>
        <span>COURAGE</span>
        <span>CONFIDENCE</span>
        <span>CREATIVITY</span>
        <span>CONNECTEDNESS</span>

      </div>

      <p>
        They may be harder to access during an episode. You can start with curiosity
        about what is happening, even when calm or compassion feels out of reach.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / PARTS -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-black" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-3-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        03 / PARTS
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-3-title">
        EVERYBODY'S<br>
        GOT A<br>
        FUCKING JOB.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <div class="ifs-parts">

        <div>
          <span>MANAGERS</span>
          <p>Try to prevent pain through control, perfectionism, criticism, or avoidance.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>FIREFIGHTERS</span>
          <p>Seek immediate relief when distress rises, sometimes through substances or impulsive behavior.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>EXILES</span>
          <p>Carry vulnerable feelings, painful memories, and beliefs about rejection or worth.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Understanding what a behavior is trying to accomplish can help you identify the
        underlying need. It does not make harmful behavior acceptable.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / BIPOLAR -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-purple" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-4-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        04 / BIPOLAR
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-4-title">
        PARTS<br>
        AREN'T<br>
        EPISODES.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        Mania, depression, and psychosis are not simply IFS parts. Mood episodes can
        intensify fears, self-criticism, urges, and internal conflict, but parts
        language does not explain away the illness.
      </p>

      <p>
        Use this framework alongside psychiatric treatment and your bipolar care plan.
        During depression, needing rest or help does not mean you must earn compassion
        through productivity.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / GET CURIOUS -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-pink" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-5-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        05 / CURIOSITY
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-5-title">
        ASK BEFORE<br>
        YOU ATTACK.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        When an urge or harsh judgment appears, explore what the part wants to protect.
        You can listen without agreeing to its preferred behavior.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-questions">

        <p>WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?</p>
        <p>WHAT ARE YOU TRYING TO DO FOR ME?</p>
        <p>WHAT DO YOU NEED ME TO UNDERSTAND?</p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / UNBLENDING -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-yellow" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-6-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        06 / UNBLENDING
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-6-title">
        STEP<br>
        BACK<br>
        A LITTLE.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        Blending is when one part’s perspective feels like your whole reality.
        Unblending means making room to notice that perspective.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-unblend">
        <div>
          <span>BLENDED</span>
          <p>“I’m a terrible person.”</p>
        </div>
        <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
        <div>
          <span>A LITTLE SPACE</span>
          <p>“A part of me feels ashamed right now.”</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Parts language is a framework. You do not need to imagine separate people inside
        your mind or force answers.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 07 / POLARIZATION -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-purple" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-7-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        07 / POLARIZED PARTS
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-7-title">
        INTERNAL<br>
        TUG OF<br>
        WAR.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        Parts can become polarized: control versus escape, independence versus support,
        sobriety versus immediate relief. Ask what each fears and needs. You can
        acknowledge both concerns while choosing behavior that protects your well-being.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 08 / COMPASSION + ACCOUNTABILITY -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-pink" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-8-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        08 / ACCOUNTABILITY
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-8-title">
        COMPASSION<br>
        ISN'T A<br>
        FREE PASS.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        Wanting relief can explain a behavior without excusing its consequences.
        Acknowledge the harm, make amends where possible, and recognize that others may
        need time to heal.
      </p>

      <p>
        Your inner critic may believe endless shame will prevent another mistake. Change
        calls for accountability, support, practical skills, and healthier ways to cope.
        You can regret a decision without condemning your entire identity.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 09 / PRACTICE -->
  <section class="ifs-section ifs-black" aria-labelledby="ifs-section-9-title">

    <div class="ifs-section-heading">
      <p class="ifs-number">
        09 / PUT IT INTO PRACTICE
      </p>

      <h2 id="ifs-section-9-title">
        WHO'S<br>
        TALKING<br>
        RIGHT NOW?
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-copy">

      <p>
        Self-leadership means letting curiosity, compassion, and grounded judgment guide
        your response. You can acknowledge conflicting needs without letting one impulse
        determine what happens next.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-practice-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>
            <strong>NOTICE.</strong><br>
            What am I feeling or wanting to do?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>
            <strong>CREATE SPACE.</strong><br>
            Try “a part of me feels…”
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>
            <strong>GET CURIOUS.</strong><br>
            What does this part fear or need?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>
            <strong>CHOOSE.</strong><br>
            What response supports my values and well-being?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>
            <strong>ACCEPT SUPPORT.</strong><br>
            Recognize when symptoms need outside help and your care plan.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="ifs-ending">

    <div>

      <p class="ifs-ending-small">
        YOU HOLD DIFFERENT NEEDS.
      </p>

      <h2>
        NONE OF THEM<br>
        ARE THE<br>
        <span>WHOLE YOU.</span>
      </h2>

    </div>

    <div class="ifs-ending-copy">

      <p>
        You do not have to hate the parts of yourself that struggle in order to change.
        Understand what is happening inside, take responsibility for what happens
        outside, and keep building a life shaped by more than your diagnosis.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO PERSPECTIVES",
          bipolar_perspectives_path,
          class: "ifs-back-button" %>

    </div>

  </section>

</main>

